/-
  Phys.Algebra.LorentzContinuumCliffordPinSurjective — N151: THE SURJECTIVITY of the
  UNIT-NORMALIZED PIN DOUBLE COVER `coverMapPinUnit ↠ SO⁺(1,9)`.
  Over the derived ℝ `Cut`, the terminal algebra `O Cut`, the spacetime `STVC`, the indefinite
  Minkowski form `BvC`, the Clifford algebra `CliffC = CliffordAlgebra QvCQuad`.
  ===========================================================================
  CONTEXT — THE OTHER HALF OF THE DOUBLE COVER (W4.5 SUFFICIENCY: advance to the genuinely-new
  datum) + THE ONE LAW reframe (the reflection is scale-invariant in its axis).

  N150 banked the EXACT KERNEL `MonoidHom.mker coverMapPinUnit = {1, -1}` — the unit-normalized
  Pin double cover `coverMapPinUnit : PinUnitSub →* bvIsomLinMonoid` is injective-mod-{±1}. That
  closed the KERNEL half of `Pin(1,9) ↠ SO⁺(1,9)`. The remaining open structure of the cover is
  its SURJECTIVITY: every Lorentz isometry is covered by a UNIT-normalized Pin element.

  ── THE ONE LAW REFRAME (trunk-native, NOT a grind). ──
  N144 (`coverMap_surjective`) already covers ALL of `SO⁺(1,9)` — but on the BLOATED domain
  `CoversSub`, whose reflection generators `cliffUnitOf a` use RAW axes of ARBITRARY norm `QvC a`.
  The literal descent to the unit-normalized domain `PinUnitSub` (generated by UNIT axes,
  `QvC a = ±1`) would seem to need an entirely new cover construction. Returning to what the
  theory says: a Householder reflection depends ONLY on the DIRECTION of its axis —
    `houseHolderM (c • a) = houseHolderM a`   for `c ≠ 0`   (`houseHolderM_smul`),
  because rescaling the axis rescales the projection coefficient `2·(BvC a a)⁻¹·BvC a p` by
  `c⁻²·c = c⁻¹` against the `c•a` factor, cancelling. So ANY anisotropic axis `a` is replaced by
  the UNIT axis `unitAxis a := (cutSqrt |QvC a|⁻¹) • a` (`QvC (unitAxis a) = sign(QvC a) = ±1`,
  via the banked scalar square root `cutSqrt`, N57, the order-completeness of the derived ℝ `Cut`),
  whose `cliffUnitOf` is a UNIT Pin GENERATOR (`pinUnitGenSet`) covering the SAME reflection
  `houseHolderM a`. Re-running the cover induction over reflection words now lands inside
  `PinUnitSub`, and N132's classification (`reflection_closure_eq_bvIsomLinMonoid`, every isometry
  IS a reflection word) + `coverOp` uniqueness give the surjectivity of `coverMapPinUnit`.

  Together with N150's kernel, `Pin(1,9) ↠ SO⁺(1,9)` is now a SURJECTIVE two-to-one group
  homomorphism — DERIVED forward, no posited Pin/Spin group, no posited cover, no posited
  surjectivity.

  ── WHAT THIS NODE BANKS ──
    QvC_smul                  — `QvC (c • a) = c·c·QvC a` (the quadratic form scales by `c²`).
    houseHolderM_smul         — ★ THE SCALE-INVARIANCE: `houseHolderM (c • a) = houseHolderM a`
                                for `c ≠ 0` — the reflection depends only on the axis DIRECTION.
    unitNormCut               — the rescale scalar `cutSqrt |QvC a|⁻¹`.
    unitNormCut_sq            — `unitNormCut a · unitNormCut a = |QvC a|⁻¹` (`cutSqrt_sq`).
    unitNormCut_pos           — `0 < unitNormCut a` for `QvC a ≠ 0` (`cutSqrt_pos`).
    unitAxis                  — the UNIT axis `unitNormCut a • a` (same direction, `QvC = ±1`).
    QvC_unitAxis              — `QvC (unitAxis a) = 1 ∨ QvC (unitAxis a) = -1` for `QvC a ≠ 0`.
    unitAxis_aniso            — `BvC (unitAxis a) (unitAxis a) ≠ 0` (the unit axis is anisotropic).
    houseHolderM_unitAxis     — `houseHolderM (unitAxis a) = houseHolderM a` (scale-invariance).
    cliffUnitOf_unitAxis_mem  — the unit-axis covering generator lands in `PinUnitSub`.
    cliffUnitOf_unitAxis_covers — it covers the SAME reflection `houseHolderM a`.
    cover_global_reflection_word_pinUnit — ★★ the reflection-word cover landing in `PinUnitSub`.
    cover_global_bvIsom_pinUnit — ★★ every `BvC`-isometry has a UNIT-normalized covering unit.
    ★★★ coverMapPinUnit_surjective — THE SURJECTIVITY `coverMapPinUnit ↠ SO⁺(1,9)`.
    coverMapPinUnit_boost_apply — W8 teeth: the concrete boost `(5/3,4/3)` is the image of a
                                UNIT-normalized Pin element.

  STANDARD (the second gate):
  • UNBROKEN — every object from the chain N49–N150 + the derived ℝ `Cut` + `cutSqrt` (N57) +
    `BvC`/`QvC`/`houseHolderM` + the cover/Pin family (N133–N146); `CliffordAlgebra`/`Submonoid`/
